    <!-- CRLF_INJECTION_LOGS on GlobalApiExceptionHandler's two log calls.
         The finding is correct in principle: the request path and the X-Correlation-Id header are
         caller-controlled, and a caller that puts a line break in either could forge log lines.
         It IS mitigated. Every value passed to a logger goes through safeForLog(), which replaces
         every control character and truncates to 200 characters, and
         GlobalApiExceptionHandlerTests.loggedValuesAreSanitised asserts that no CR or LF survives
         into a formatted log message.
         findsecbugs cannot see that. Its taint analysis does not follow a sanitiser into a helper
         method, and inlining the same replaceAll at the call site does not satisfy it either: the
         detector flags any value derived from getRequestURI() regardless of what happens in
         between. Suppressed here with the mitigation named rather than weakening the gate or
         dropping the logging that makes a 500 diagnosable at all. -->
    <Match>
        <Class name="com.fitsync.web.error.GlobalApiExceptionHandler"/>
        <Bug pattern="CRLF_INJECTION_LOGS"/>
    </Match>

